				<div id="essay">
					<h2>A softball sensation</h2>
					<p>By the time Angelina was eleven, she had five seasons of softball experience, including two on an all-star team. But like so many others, she didn&#8217;t start out being a great ballplayer.</p>
					<p class="pullquote">As Angelina watched the other softball players, she decided that she wanted to be just as good.</p>
					<p>At her first day of T-ball practice, Angelina was one of only two girls on her team. She couldn&#8217;t catch, throw, or hit the ball. When she came home from practice, she said, &#8220;I&#8217;ll never be able to do this.&#8221;  Her parents encouraged her to keep trying, telling her that she could do anything.</p>
					<p>As Angelina watched the other softball players, she decided that she wanted to be just as good. Angelina made certain she was ready for practices, glove always in hand. Before dinner, she would play catch with her dad. Each year, she showed improvement.</p>
					<p>In spring 2007, Angelina joined a recreational team. She would encourage the younger girls to get to practice on time and warm up. She always gave support and demonstrated how they could improve&#8212;how to hold their gloves, get under the ball, and always use two hands to catch it.</p>
					<p>One day, Angelina was asked to take over as catcher of her team. She wasn&#8217;t sure she wanted to catch, but she took extra practice with her dad at the field to improve her throw to second base and learn how to make the out at home plate.</p>
					<p class="last">When Angelina played shortstop with the all-star team, she received the Most-Valuable-Player award at a tournament. Carrying the plaque back to the dugout, she spoke with her coach, who told the team Angelina had an announcement. She said she felt someone else on the team deserved it more because of how much she had improved her game, and gave the plaque to a teammate.  Angelina once again showed why she&#8217;ll always be most valuable in her team and in her  family&#8217;s hearts.</p>
				</div>
